#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Perspectives on how to start your quantum initiative. This includes "
"developing a vision, mission statement, and focus areas."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Early stages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore upskilled */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Build your quantum program {#build-your-quantum-program}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The development of an organization's quantum initiatives will be influenced "
"by a variety of factors, including research goals, and human and fiscal "
"resources. Early-stage development often consists of steps that include: 1) "
"establish a vision, mission and focus area, 2) you onboard your own team, 3)"
" enable that team (to build in that focus area), and then 4) evaluate the "
"focus area and your team's progress and iterate the process of narrowing or "
"shifting focus and the corresponding team enablement. Let's explore what "
"some of these steps mean.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Define mission statement:** Define the overarching and high-level vision "
"for program and team activities; create a path towards achieving the shared "
"vision through a clear and prescriptive mission and objectives.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Define goals and their measures of success:** Identify goals that "
"contribute to the mission. Define a process and metrics to assess and "
"determine success of the identified goals. The field of quantum computing "
"changes rapidly. So having big-picture priorities and criteria for success "
"clearly defined can be instrumental when technology or interest changes. "
"Identify what programs, events and resources (either from IBM Quantum&reg; "
"or of your own) will be crucial in advancing your goals.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Define research and application focus areas:** Quantum computing has "
"applications in so many areas. That's part of its appeal. But it also means "
"we have to make tough choices in picking one or two focus areas to have a "
"deep impact. Align team capabilities, resources, drivers, and mission to a "
"focus area that targets near-term quantum advantage. Define a process for "
"evaluation and iterative development on project focus areas based on "
"discoveries.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Build an interdisciplinary team:** Build a team on which many different "
"backgrounds and fields of expertise are represented. Partners commonly "
"identify backgrounds in physics, programming, business, project management, "
"and marketing as being critical. Define how the team will work together in "
"pursuit of team goals through assignment of roles and responsibilities.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Onboard and enable the team:** Guide and coach individuals based on their "
"unique background and quantum computing goals. Direct team members to the "
"[IBM Quantum Learning platform](/learning) for courses, tutorials, and "
"documentation, and also be sure to take advantage of any IBM Quantum live "
"events to which you have access. These resources will help your team fast-"
"track and simplify their quantum computing learning journey.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following sections will add detail to the guidelines 1-3 above. Items "
"4-5 will be addressed in the next lesson.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Establish a vision and mission {#establish-a-vision-and-mission}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The field of quantum computing is developing rapidly. This makes it "
"important to have guiding priorities and clear criteria for success.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We recommend you start by defining your organization's quantum computing vision and mission to guide and direct your organization to success. \n"
"    A **vision** defines an aspirational long-term goal and future state. \n"
"    A **mission** charts the path towards achieving a vision by defining the current near-term purpose, objectives, and required actions. \n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The vision and mission collectively serve as your team's lighthouse, guiding"
" your team to achieve near-term and long-term success based on your "
"organization's values, priorities, and strategy.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Identify goals {#identify-goals}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once you have determined your organization's quantum vision and mission, define goals that ladder up to your organization's vision and mission. \n"
"    Goals exist across many dimensions. Four dimensions in particular have proved useful to many partners in helping them define the high-level priorities of their teams. We recommend prioritizing at most two dimensions to facilitate success.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Business Impact\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Education & Talent Development\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "External Eminence\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Scientific Advancement\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Afterwards, re-visit your quantum mission statement to ensure the identified"
" objectives and dimensions promote your mission statement.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, align your goals with the tools available through IBM Quantum to help "
"your organization achieve your goals. Map each goal to a benefit to identify"
" advancers of the goal. If you are a partner in the IBM Quantum Network, "
"work with your dedicated IBM Quantum team to identify the benefits that "
"serve your goals the best.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once all drivers (mission, objectives, and values) have been identified, "
"work to create a viable action plan to drive accountability, transparency, "
"and motivation across your organization based on the current state of your "
"capabilities and resources.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Examples {#examples}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The example value maps below are informed by real cases from the IBM Quantum"
" Network, though they are not taken from any single partner's workshop. Most"
" organizations assign some non-zero value to all four dimensions, as they "
"are clearly interconnected. For example, one cannot have a large business "
"impact using quantum computing if there is not a quantum-smart workforce "
"from which to hire. But an enterprise may still choose to prioritize "
"business impact, while academic institutions may choose to prioritize "
"workforce training and education.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first image corresponds to an organization that is focused on having a "
"business impact through the development of new quantum-based technology, "
"such as algorithm development or optimization methods for using quantum "
"hardware. \n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![This is a diagram of priorities. There are four axes: business impact, "
"eminence and industry leadership, scientific advancement, and education and "
"workforce development. Business impact and scientific advancement are most "
"heavily weighted.](/learning/images/courses/designing-and-leading-quantum-"
"projects/early-stages/priorities1.svg)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This second value map is a composite of institutions focused on eminence and"
" business impact. Success for such an institution might include speaking at "
"an IBM Quantum event and one regional quantum event, to build eminence. With"
" business impact in mind, success for this institution could be identifying "
"use cases regarding current business problems and delivering a proof of "
"concept based on one of the identified use cases.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![This is a diagram of priorities. There are four axes: business impact, "
"eminence and industry leadership, scientific advancement, and education and "
"workforce development. Business impact and eminence are most heavily "
"weighted.](/learning/images/courses/designing-and-leading-quantum-"
"projects/early-stages/priorities2.svg)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Priorities {#priorities}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once concrete goals are in place, it is time to prioritize them, and to "
"decide what success looks like. Each theme of guiding priorities is paired "
"with potential metrics and measures of success. Some wording may be more "
"appropriate for one partner type or another (such as a QIC having "
"\"members\").\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Priorities of an organization and what metrics of success they might "
"use.](/learning/images/courses/designing-and-leading-quantum-projects/early-"
"stages/value-drivers-metrics.svg)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Key points**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Keep things simple - focus on problems most interesting/useful to customers "
"or closely related to your core competencies.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Leverage state of the art methods in quantum computing, while also exploring"
" new avenues for growth with the technology.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Actively talk to a wide range of customers/stakeholders and quantum "
"ecosystem members.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Stay up to date on news regarding hardware and software developers, as well "
"as universities and national labs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Implement iterative development (agile methodology) for priorities, values, "
"and focus areas.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Metrics of success {#metrics-of-success}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because quantum computing is such a rapidly-changing field, it is critical "
"to choose metrics of success that can adjust to a moving target, but which "
"will also correspond to some reliable deliverable.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is a short list of common metrics used by leaders of successful quantum"
" initiatives.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Number of team members upskilled to the level of quantum expertise (building"
" skills to experiment in quantum computing)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Number of research papers (advancing science and technology)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Number of students and workforce members trained\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Number of patents or potentially patentable assets (IP and algorithm "
"portfolio)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Number of business use cases you can deliver quantum-ready\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Number of quantum-aware employees in the client organization (such as "
"through light training like [Quantum Business "
"Foundations](/learning/courses/quantum-business-foundations))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Number of events organized and executed\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Number of active users on IBM Quantum Platform\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Number of speaking events (internal/external)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Research or application focus {#research-or-application-focus}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This lesson has been primarily about focusing your quantum initiative. Let "
"us think about what that means in the context of research. One reason that "
"quantum is so appealing is its potential to fundamentally alter an amazing "
"breadth of fields and industries. But that breadth of possibility can also "
"hinder success, if a quantum team does not focus on one area (or a few well-"
"defined areas). It is therefore critical to pick an area of research and "
"application, early on.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How do you define a research focus? This will have obvious interplay with "
"the make-up of your team and their expertise, as well as with the core goals"
" of your organization, such as focusing on fundamental research versus "
"industry applications. The following steps helped prior partners define a "
"research focus.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Start with your comfort zone(s) and branch out.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Being an IBM Quantum Network partner positions you to note and leverage "
"similarities between challenges in different fields and economic sectors.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Listen to your stakeholders.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Prioritize based on potential impact.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition to the steps above, there are considerations unique to "
"organizations working with clients, such as the following:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Start outreach to potential clients/partners early**: Member agreements "
"for QICs can take a long time to work out. Other client engagements may be "
"similar. Having several strong candidates lined up prior to starting system "
"access can help the launch of a quantum initiative to build momentum.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Refine member/client engagement models**: What works for a member or "
"client at one stage won't work in all stages. You may need to revisit your "
"engagement model, and revise things like frequency or modality of "
"meetings.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the next lesson we will discuss assembling a team, including key roles "
"and responsibilities.\n"
msgstr ""
